## Incident Report: Network Forensic Analysis

Based on my analysis of the PCAP file, I have identified a confirmed infostealer infection on the network. Below is the comprehensive incident report with all evidence-backed indicators of compromise.

```json
{
  "victim": {
    "ip": "10.1.21.58",
    "mac": "00:21:5d:c8:0e:f2",
    "hostname": "DESKTOP-ES9F3ML",
    "user": "gwyatt"
  },
  "malware_family": "Vidar Infostealer",
  "attribution_confidence": "behavioral",
  "iocs": [
    {
      "type": "c2_endpoint",
      "value": "153.92.1.49:443",
      "evidence": "18 TCP SYN connections from victim to this IP on port 443 (TLS); host resolves to whitepepper.su; tshark: tcp.flags.syn==1 shows repeated C2 beacon pattern"
    },
    {
      "type": "c2_endpoint",
      "value": "153.92.1.49:80",
      "evidence": "6 TCP SYN connections from victim to this IP on port 80 (HTTP); unencrypted C2 communication; tshark conversation analysis"
    },
    {
      "type": "domain",
      "value": "whitepepper.su",
      "evidence": "C2 domain identified in TLS SNI and HTTP Host headers; tshark: tls.handshake.extensions_server_name==whitepepper.su and http.host==whitepepper.su for 153.92.1.49"
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "value": "http://whitepepper.su/api/set_agent?id=3BF67EC05320C5729578BE4C0ADF174C&token=842e2802df0f0a06b4ed51f12f4387e761523b&description=&agent=Chrome",
      "evidence": "GET request frame 24500; agent registration endpoint; tshark: http.request.full_uri extraction"
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "value": "http://whitepepper.su/api/set_agent?id=3BF67EC05320C5729578BE4C0ADF174C&token=842e2802df0f0a06b4ed51f12f4387e761523b&description=&agent=Chrome&act=log",
      "evidence": "POST request frame 24601; command execution logging; tshark: http.request.method==POST filter"
    },
    {
      "type": "url",
      "value": "http://whitepepper.su/api/set_agent?id=3BF67EC05320C5729578BE4C0ADF174C&token=842e2802df0f0a06b4ed51f12f4387e761523b&description=&agent=Edge&act=log",
      "evidence": "POST request frame 25286; Edge browser credential theft; identical C2 pattern to Chrome registration"
    },
    {
      "type": "file_hash",
      "value": "e2935b5b28550d47dc971f456d6961f20d1633b4892998750140e0eaa9ae9d78",
      "evidence": "PE32 DLL executable disguised as JPEG; filename 5(1).jpg in HTTP export; tshark --export-objects http"
    },
    {
      "type": "file_hash",
      "value": "1d48d9166408d8b8bf39f9557e4f8a57133c353567c55966ec2831a7bc230431",
      "evidence": "PE32+ x86-64 executable (possibly malware loader); filename am_delta_patch_1.349.439.0_dcf977cccce1b58289d270f71f8151b3acc1566b(8).exe; file command output"
    },
    {
      "type": "file_hash",
      "value": "0fb4d47bcda9b77b0fbd8cb88b34ba180365991f6a376e00add1ac880b67fd8f",
      "evidence": "PE32+ executable variant (different export); filename am_delta_patch_1.349.439.0_dcf977cccce1b58289d270f71f8151b3acc1566b(4).exe; tshark extraction"
    },
    {
      "type": "file_name",
      "value": "5(1).jpg",
      "evidence": "Masqueraded PE32 DLL payload; tshark --export-objects extracted from HTTP stream; likely infostealer module"
    },
    {
      "type": "domain",
      "value": "cloudflare-ech.com",
      "evidence": "Spoofed Cloudflare domain; resolves to 104.21.46.67; TLS SNI field; 16 MB data exfiltration from victim; likely malware distribution server"
    },
    {
      "type": "domain",
      "value": "communicationfirewall-security.cc",
      "evidence": "Phishing/malware domain; TLS handshake from victim to 104.21.9.36; domain mimics legitimate firewall/security vendor"
    },
    {
      "type": "domain",
      "value": "media.megafilehub4.lat",
      "evidence": "Suspicious file hosting domain; TLS handshake from victim to 104.21.48.156; consistent with malware infrastructure"
    }
  ],
  "benign_context": [
    "Google Safe Browsing, YouTube, Gmail, Maps, Fonts APIs (standard Windows 11 telemetry)",
    "Microsoft Bing, OneDrive, Windows Update services (expected for Windows 11 Enterprise workstation)",
    "Active Directory LDAP queries to domain controller 10.1.21.2 on port 389 (normal AD auth)",
    "Kerberos authentication to domain via port 88 (normal domain-joined Windows behavior)",
    "Google connectivity test via clients2.google.com (Windows network detection)"
  ],
  "incident_summary": "The Windows 11 workstation DESKTOP-ES9F3ML (10.1.21.58, user gwyatt) was infected with Vidar infostealer malware. The malware performed browser credential theft targeting Chrome and Edge, registered itself with a C2 server at whitepepper.su (153.92.1.49), and exfiltrated system fingerprinting data via HTTP-based C2 protocol. Three PE32/PE32+ executables were downloaded and executed, indicating multi-stage infection chain with delivery from spoofed domains (cloudflare-ech.com, communicationfirewall-security.cc, media.megafilehub4.lat)."
}
